  "signals": "Every circuit here brings two kinds of signal into one block. A block reads each input as its own kind: a bit block sees a digit as 1 unless it's 0, a solid shape as 1 and a wave as 1 while it's above the middle; a digit block sees a shape as its corners and a wave as a digit, 0 at the bottom and 9 at the top; a shape block sees anything else as a circle, solid for anything but 0.",
